# Mandatory Test Orchestration Runner (N78-TEST-001)

**Registry rule ID:** **FAMILY-N78-TEST-001** (GATE). **Standard ID:** N78-TEST-001.

## Policy and compliance rule

- **Enforcement:** Strict — evidence required before **PASS** (internal policy label: *fail-closed*). Missing, skipped, or failing applicable layers block release; do not treat that as a failed test run by itself.
- Any change (feature, refactor, bug fix) MUST execute all three required layers applicable to that change:
  1. **Logic and calculation tests**
  2. **Rendered-UI tests**
  3. **Device / target-runtime tests**
- Never declare **PASS** if any applicable layer is missing, unexecuted, skipped, or failing.
- Never weaken, bypass, or delete existing assertions or tests to green a gate.
- Question-only or review-only turns with **no** production/test harness changes: orchestration may be **NOT APPLICABLE** — say so explicitly; do not invent PASS.

## Orchestration workflow

Before completing any task that changes behavior, run the project-appropriate orchestrator in the terminal (or the smallest focused subset that still covers every affected layer).

### Discovery and verification commands

Detect harnesses and run the correct lane:

| Stack | Layer 1 — Logic | Layer 2 — Rendered UI | Layer 3 — Device / runtime |
| ----- | ----------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------- |
| **Gradle / KMP** | `gradlew.bat` / `gradlew` — `allTests`, `:shared:desktopTest`, `:common:testDebugUnitTest`, or product doc | Compose `desktopTest`, Android `androidTest`, screen-reading suite | `connectedDebugAndroidTest`, `:desktop:visibleUiQa`, or product on-screen orchestrator |
| **npm / Node** | `npm run test:logic` or `npm test` | `npm run test:ui` | `npm run test:e2e` or `npm run test:all` |
| **Python** | `pytest` (unit paths) | integration/UI paths per project | E2E per product QA doc |

On **Windows**, prefer `gradlew.bat` and `pwsh -NoProfile -File tools/...` from the product repo root.

Inspect exit codes and JUnit (or equivalent) XML. Fix failures; do not suppress.

Each product MUST document a release orchestrator (`run-*-qa-suite.ps1`, `*ReleaseGate.bat`, or equivalent) that maps the three layers when the product ships user-facing behavior.

## Required compliance output

When behavior or tests changed, end the turn with:

```text
N78-TEST-001 compliance
Standard: N78-TEST-001
Enforcement: Strict (evidence required — no PASS without executed tests)
Change scope: [one line]

Layer 1 — Logic:          PASS | FAIL | NOT VERIFIED | N/A
  Command(s):
  Evidence:

Layer 2 — Rendered UI:    PASS | FAIL | NOT VERIFIED | N/A
  Command(s):
  Evidence:

Layer 3 — Device/runtime: PASS | FAIL | NOT VERIFIED | N/A
  Command(s):
  Evidence:

Regression / guardrails:  PASS | FAIL | NOT VERIFIED | N/A
  Command(s):

Artifacts: [paths to reports/logs]

Final status: PASS | FAIL | NOT VERIFIED
Blockers: [if not PASS]
```

**PASS** only when every applicable layer is **PASS** with execution evidence. **No test evidence, no PASS.**
